# License — Split by Artifact Type

This repository uses a split license: skill *content* is copyleft (attribution +
share-alike) so it stays open and credited, while *tooling* is permissive (MIT)
so integrators have no copyleft surprises.

## Skill content — CC BY-SA 4.0

The following are licensed under
[Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International](./LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt):

- `skills/**/SKILL.md`
- Documentation prose in `docs/**`

**Attribution is required.** Derivative works must be shared under the same
license. Most skills in this catalog include a portable footer with the
attribution + license obligation rendered in-place — keep it intact when
redistributing.

## Tooling and code — MIT

The following are licensed under [MIT](./LICENSES/MIT.txt):

- `scripts/**` (validators, link-checkers, CI helpers)
- `tests/**`
- Config files

## External contributions

By submitting a pull request to this repository, contributors agree their
contribution will be licensed under the same split: skill content under
CC BY-SA 4.0, tooling under MIT.

## Questions

If a file's licensing is unclear, the per-directory rules above govern. When
in doubt, treat it as CC BY-SA 4.0 (the more restrictive of the two).

Contact: <oji@productmind.co>
